  "notes": "Agent re-read after the Code Health refactor, 2026-11-07, under the owner directive transcribed in verification/reviews/rulings/agent-rereview-after-refactor-2026-11-07.md. This record is NOT an owner signature: it attests the agent's substantive reading only. Read proxy.trust_plan and proxy.trust_plan_co_provenance. TrustPlan still has no reload field: reload() is trust_reload_plan over the revocation state. Other merged work (#1251) replaced the two handed-in values, the response issuer kid and the epoch, with one sealed ResponseAuthority produced only by startup_plan::response_authority_plans; TrustPlan::from_validated takes it whole, so the statement's 'cannot become the authority for the values it is handed' holds with one argument where it said two, and the test the claim cites for it is now startup_plan::response_authority::tests::the_trust_plan_carries_the_authority_it_is_handed. The claim, premises and dependencies are unchanged. Evidence class as registered; V0 units are tested and probed, not machine-checked proofs. The mutation lane was not re-run by this reading; check-registries resolves every probe anchor, and every tested symbol the unit names still names a test function. The previous record named the owner as reviewer; it is replaced because its fingerprint no longer matched the tree, and it remains in git history. Owner ratification of this reading is the owner's act.",
